Let a session advertise NV12 and P010 dmabufs again

Hyprland 0.57 stopped advertising every YUV format over linux-dmabuf, because
its external-texture shader draws them without converting to RGB
(hyprwm/Hyprland#16570, for discussion #16420). That is right for surfaces,
but some clients need the format advertised only to allocate buffers they
never attach to a surface. Chromium's VA-API video encoder is one: under
Linux it takes its input only as NV12 dmabufs, and Ozone/Wayland refuses to
allocate a format the compositor does not advertise, so every hardware encode
fails on its first frame ("Unable to create a mappable shared image").

Add an opt-in, HYPRLAND_EGL_ADVERTISE_NV12, read like the existing
HYPRLAND_EGL_NO_MODIFIERS. When set, NV12 and P010 pass the filter in
initDRMFormats() and a warning is logged; the scanout feedback keeps leaving
YUV out. Unset, nothing changes. A client that does attach such a buffer to a
surface is still drawn with wrong colours, which is why this is not the
default.

--- a/src/render/OpenGL.cpp
+++ b/src/render/OpenGL.cpp
@@ -532,6 +532,13 @@
     if (DISABLE_MODS)
         LOG(Log::WARN, "HYPRLAND_EGL_NO_MODIFIERS set, disabling modifiers");
 
+    // YUV is not advertised because the renderer cannot draw it yet. Some clients
+    // need NV12 or P010 advertised only to allocate buffers they never attach to
+    // a surface: Chromium's VA-API video encoder takes its input that way.
+    const auto ADVERTISE_NV12 = Env::envEnabled("HYPRLAND_EGL_ADVERTISE_NV12");
+    if (ADVERTISE_NV12)
+        LOG(Log::WARN, "HYPRLAND_EGL_ADVERTISE_NV12 set, advertising NV12 and P010; a surface using them is drawn with wrong colors");
+
     if (!m_exts.EXT_image_dma_buf_import) {
         LOG(Log::ERR, "EGL: No dmabuf import, DMABufs will not work.");
         return;
@@ -571,7 +578,7 @@
 
     for (auto const& fmt : formats) {
         // Do not advertise YUV until the renderer supports it.
-        if (NFormatUtils::isFormatYUV(fmt))
+        if (NFormatUtils::isFormatYUV(fmt) && !(ADVERTISE_NV12 && (fmt == DRM_FORMAT_NV12 || fmt == DRM_FORMAT_P010)))
             continue;
 
         std::vector<uint64_t> mods;
